  "hints": [
    "scanning nums2 in full for every element of nums1 is doing the same membership check over and over. what structure gives O(1) membership checks?",
    "put every value from nums1 into a hash set",
    "scan nums2 once, and for each value, check if it's in the set - if so, add it to your result set (to naturally avoid duplicates) and remove it from the lookup set so it isn't added twice",
    "sort the final result before returning, since the problem asks for ascending order"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting to deduplicate the result when the same overlapping value appears multiple times in either array",
    "not sorting the final result",
    "building the set from the larger array when it would be more efficient to build it from the smaller one (a performance detail, not a correctness one, but worth noticing)"
  ],
